{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 20,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore do my thoughts cause me to answer, and for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I make haste.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have heard the check of my reproach, and the spirit of my understanding causeth me to answer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowest thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this of old, since man was placed upon earth,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the triumphing of the wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " short, and the joy of the hypocrite ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for a moment?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though his excellence shall mount up to the heavens, and his head reach to the clouds;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he shall perish for ever like his own dung: they who have seen him shall say, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall fly away as a dream, and will not be found: yea, he shall be chased away as a vision of the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The eye also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " saw him shall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "see him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no more; neither shall his place any more behold him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His children shall seek to please the poor, and his hands shall restore their goods.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His bones are full ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the sin",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of his youth, which shall lie down with him in the dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though wickedness may be sweet in his mouth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "though",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he may hide it under his tongue;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he may spare it, and forsake it not; but keep it still within his mouth:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his food in his bowels is turned, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the gall of asps within him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath swallowed down riches, and he shall vomit them up again: God shall cast them out of his belly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall suck the poison of asps: the viper's tongue shall slay him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not see the river, the floods, the brooks of honey and buttermilk.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which he labored for shall he restore, and shall not swallow ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": according to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " substance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the restitution ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and he shall not rejoice ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because he hath oppressed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath forsaken the poor; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "because",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hath violently taken away a house which he did not build.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely he shall not feel quietness in his belly, he shall not save of that which he desired.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There shall none of his food be left; therefore shall no man look for his goods.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the fullness of his sufficiency he shall be in straits: every hand of the wicked shall come upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he is about to fill his belly, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall cast the fury of his wrath upon him, and shall rain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon him while he is eating.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall flee from the iron weapon, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the bow of steel shall strike him through.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is drawn, and cometh out of the body; yes, the glittering sword cometh out of his gall: terrors ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All darkness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hid in his secret places: a fire not blown shall consume him; it shall go ill with him that is left in his tabernacle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heaven shall reveal his iniquity; and the earth shall rise up against him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The increase of his house shall depart, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and his goods",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall flow away in the day of his wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.20.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.20.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the portion of a wicked man from God, and the heritage appointed to him by God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
